N : what do you want? 
Evan pushes a hand through his greasy hair , peering at you over his glasses .
P : you’re in an awfully good mood.
the nerd snorts as he rolls his eyes at your sarcasm . 
N : I think I’ve earned the right to be in a bad mood , considering there is a corpse in the dining room and we’re trapped here .
P : fair , fair . 
N : I told you guys from the start , a reunion trip is a terrible idea , but nooooo , it’d be soooo fun , Evan, just take some time out of your incredulously  busy schedule to -
P : I don’t think you could’ve predicted this would happen.]
he flushes at your interruption .
N : irregardless! it would’ve been disastrous, group vacations always are . though I must admit , I did not expect things to become so ..
for a moment , Evan seemed genuinely at a loss for words . which was strange, since he normally never managed to keep his mouth shut for more than 10 consecutive minutes .
you nod in response , any comfort you could give him gets caught in your throat . 
P : …. soooo -
Evan cuts you off , his expression returning to one of irritation . 
N : what is it ? 
P : yeah , I just wanted to ask you -
